/P 5058 0 R
/E (This course provides a comprehensive introduction to computer systems and networks, covering both hardware and software aspects. Students gain a deep understanding of the fundamental principles, architectures, and protocols that underpin modern computing systems including CPU and GPU architectures, memory hierarchy, I/O devices, operating system concepts, process and memory management, file systems and device management The course also covers network fundamentals, diverse protocols, and in-depth analysis of network types. Advanced topics cover wireless networks, cybersecurity, cloud computing and emerging technologies particularly quantum computing. At the end of this course, students are equipped with the knowledge and skills necessary to design, implement, and manage computer systems and networks effectively.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [23]
>>
