<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 5066 0 R
/E (This course is designed to provide students with a comprehensive understanding of basic rules of probability, and statistical inference which are fundamental statistical principles behind machine learning. Students will be able to use them in modelling uncertainty in obtaining and recording data. They will be able to utilize graphical and numerical summaries of data in understanding data-generating processes, and understand the logic of statistical inference, and will be able to apply common inferential procedures. Students also will be exposed to the computational aspects of statistics using data analysis software. Topics include conditional probability, random variables, probability distributions, the law of large numbers, convergence, limiting distributions, central limit theorem, point and interval estimation, and hypothesis testing.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
