1748 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 5069 0 R
/E (This course underscores the theoretical and practical aspects of data structure concepts, accompanied by detailed algorithms for each data structure. Students will gain proficiency in abstract data-type concepts through class-based learning and subsequently apply these concepts in the implementation of data structures. Additionally, the course covers recursive programming techniques and algorithm efficiency analysis employing asymptotic notation \(Big O/Omega/Theta\). Various sorting and searching techniques will be explored as fundamental operations within data structures, accompanied by an in-depth efficiency analysis of each algorithm. Furthermore, the course delves into linear data structures such as linked lists, stacks, and queues, while also introducing non-linear data structures like trees and binary search trees. Ultimately, upon completion of this course, students are expected to enhance their digital skills significantly.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
