/E (This course provides a comprehensive introduction to computer vision. Computer vision involves the development of techniques and algorithms that enable machines to interpret and understand visual information from the world. Students will learn basic concepts of computer vision as well as hands-on experience to solve real-life vision problems. Computer vision involves the development of techniques and algorithms that enable machines to interpret and understand visual information from the world. The course covers fundamental principles, techniques, and applications of computer vision, equipping students with the knowledge and skills necessary to explore this rapidly evolving field. Major topics include image processing, detection and recognition, geometry-based and physics-based vision and video analysis.)
