/E (This course introduces students to the basic principles underlying the design and analysis related to robotic systems. Students are introduced to various classifications, types and components \(e.g. sensors, controller, actuator, etc.\) of robots. The robot modelling and design specification are also discussed. By adapting the knowledge obtained, students will be able to apply the robot models as well as be able to correctly design and simulate data-driven robot trajectory and motion planning. This course also helps students to understand and use concepts, theory, and algorithms of Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) related to robotics.          )
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
endobj
