/E (This course introduces students to the exciting and rapidly evolving field of Extended Reality \(XR\), encompassing Virtual Reality \(VR\), Augmented Reality \(AR\), and Mixed Reality \(MR\). Students will explore the theoretical foundations, technical aspects, and practical applications of XR technologies. Through a combination of lectures, hands-on projects, and discussions, students will gain a comprehensive understanding of XR and its impact on various industries. At the end of the course, students should be able to work collaboratively and create XR Content for practical applications, demonstrating the ability to create immersive and interactive experiences in virtual and augmented environments.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [26]
>>
